/Title (1. Correlation between real estate prices and national economy:  The financial crisis of 2008 has demonstrated a direct link between the ability of the public to afford their mortgage, and, the economic state of the country. This makes real estate prices an key indicator of underlying economic issues in the country, making data analysis in the field a valuable tool for the US Government in managing its economy)
